'''Wulfgar''', an [[Skyrim:Elder|elderly]] [[Skyrim:Priest|priest]], is one of the reclusive [[Skyrim:Greybeards|Greybeards]] living at the monastery at [[Skyrim:High Hrothgar|High Hrothgar]], and one of your initial tutors in the [[Lore:Way of the Voice|Way of the Voice]]. Wulfgar will react when interacted with, greeting you with a muttered ''"Dovahkiin"'' and causing the surroundings to rumble in doing so.

He wears a set of [[Skyrim:Greybeard's Robes|Greybeard's robes]] with the matching [[Skyrim:Greybeard's Hood|hood]] and [[Skyrim:Greybeard's Boots|boots]]. He carries a [[Skyrim:Wooden Bowl|wooden bowl]], a [[Skyrim:Knife (item)|knife]] and a [[Skyrim:Fork (item)|fork]], a [[Skyrim:Quill|quill]], a [[Skyrim:Roll of Paper|roll of paper]], a [[Skyrim:Nirnroot|nirnroot]], a [[Skyrim:Potato|potato]], a [[Skyrim:Venison Chop|venison chop]], a jar of [[Skyrim:Honey|honey]], a [[Skyrim:Goat Cheese Wedge|goat cheese wedge]], and a piece of [[Skyrim:Bread|bread]].

Wulfgar knows the following shouts: [[Skyrim:Disarm|Disarm]], [[Skyrim:Dismay|Dismay]], [[Skyrim:Elemental Fury|Elemental Fury]], [[Skyrim:Fire Breath|Fire Breath]], [[Skyrim:Frost Breath|Frost Breath]], [[Skyrim:Ice Form|Ice Form]], [[Skyrim:Unrelenting Force|Unrelenting Force]], and [[Skyrim:Whirlwind Sprint|Whirlwind Sprint]].

